        defendant: [.direct("Describe your life and business for the jury.", "\"I own a boat dealership at the lake. {V} and I built it together. I loved {V}, and I was devastated.\""), .direct("Where were you that evening?", "\"At the marina office. I was working late. I called 911 as soon as I learned of the shooting.\""), .direct("Why did your code enter the boathouse at 8:12?", "\"The code is shared with six staff. I do not know who used it. I did not enter the boathouse that night.\""), .direct("What about the forged loan papers?", "\"I did not forge {V}'s signature. I cannot say who signed. Someone else may have.\""), .direct("Why was a pistol in a storage locker?", "\"The locker is in my business name, but several people had access. I did not put a pistol there.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I feel destroyed. I lost my spouse, and now I am accused of the killing. I did not do it.\""), .cross("Your code entered the boathouse at 8:12 p.m., didn't it?", "\"The log says so. The code is mine, but it is shared with six staff members, and I was at the marina office.\""), .cross("You called 911 at 10:05 p.m., didn't you?", "\"Yes. As soon as I learned of the shooting. I stayed on the line until deputies arrived.\""), .cross("A lender found a forged signature of {V} on loan papers, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is what the lender found. I did not sign for {V}, and I cannot explain it.\""), .cross("A cleaned pistol was in a locker rented in your business name, wasn't it?", "\"So I am told. Several people had access to the locker, and I did not put it there.\""), .cross("{V} had asked the lender for copies that week, hadn't {V}?", "\"Yes. That is what the lender says. I did not know about the request until later.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} owns a well-known boat dealership at a lake. At 10:05 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} called 911 to say {V}, {D}'s spouse, had been shot in the family boathouse. A smart lock recorded {D}'s personal code entering at 8:12 p.m., and a lender had found a forged signature of {V} on loan papers.", "The defense will present boathouse codes shared with six staff, a fired yard hand who threatened {V} and was later arrested with a matching pistol, and no weapon or residue on {D}. The State must prove it was {D}."),
        closings: ("A code entered at 8:12 p.m., forged loan papers, a cleaned pistol in a locker rented in {D}'s business name, and a 911 call that placed {D} at the marina. {V} had asked for copies that week.", "Codes shared with six staff, a fired yard hand who threatened {V} and was arrested with a matching pistol, and no weapon or residue on {D}. The State has not proved that {D} shot {V}."),
