        exam: [.direct("How would you describe your job as an animal control officer?", "\"I respond to calls about animal neglect and cruelty. I check conditions, assess animals, and work with veterinarians.\""), .direct("How did you learn about the dog on {DATE}?", "\"A meter reader heard barking from a closed garage and called animal control.\""), .direct("What did you find?", "\"{D}'s shepherd mix in a crate with an empty water bottle in 104-degree air. The dog was panting and weak.\""), .direct("What did the veterinary report show?", "\"Heat stress, with a body temperature of 106. The dog recovered with cooling.\""), .direct("Where was {D}?", "\"At work. {D} was away from home for the day.\""), .direct("What did a neighbor say?", "\"The dog was left in the garage for ten hours most weekdays. I noted that in my report.\""), .cross("Was there a fan?", "\"{D} says a fan ran on a timer. The electric company logged an outage at 10:40 a.m. that stopped the fan.\""), .cross("Was there a water bottle?", "\"{D} says a full water bottle was clipped to the crate. I found an empty one in the crate.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D} came home as soon as called and took responsibility. {D} said {D} left water and a fan.\""), .cross("Did the dog recover?", "\"Yes. The dog recovered fully after cooling. It was a close call, but it recovered.\""), .cross("Did you find prior complaints?", "\"Only the neighbor's statement. I did not find a prior record of neglect.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} left a dog in a hot garage without water.", "A fan and a full bottle undone by a power outage."),
