        theory: ("{D} moved trip deposits to a personal card.", "A treasurer who repaid out-of-pocket uniform costs."),
        allocution: "\"I took the money. I'm sorry to the kids.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} spent the transfers on online shopping and a vacation rental.", "Uniform invoices show {DL} fronted $1,800 from personal funds."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please tell us about your work for the club.", "\"I volunteered as treasurer for years. I paid bills, kept books, and bought uniforms for students.\""), .direct("Why did you move the money to your personal card?", "\"I fronted $1,800 for uniforms from my own funds. I took the money to repay myself, and I should have asked.\""), .direct("Did you use it for uniforms?", "\"Some of it. I also spent some on online shopping and a vacation rental. I know that was wrong.\""), .direct("Did you plan to repay the club?", "\"Yes. I planned to repay what was not for uniforms. I did not do it in time.\""), .direct("Why did the charter get canceled?", "\"The deposit was not paid on time. I should have paid it first, and I did not.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"Ashamed, more than anything. I let down students and families. I wish I had been honest.\""), .cross("You moved $3,600 to your personal card, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know I did not have permission for all of it.\""), .cross("You spent part on shopping and a vacation rental, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know that was not for the club.\""), .cross("The board did not approve the transfers, did it?", "\"No. I did not ask. I own that.\""), .cross("The bus charter was canceled for nonpayment, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. Because the deposit was not paid. I take responsibility.\""), .cross("You fronted $1,800 for uniforms, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That is true. But I took more than that.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, treasurer of a high school band booster club, controlled the account for the spring trip. On {DATE}, the bus company canceled the charter for nonpayment, and the club learned $3,600 in trip deposits had been moved to {D}'s personal card.", "The defense will present uniforms that {D} paid for out of pocket, invoices for $1,800, and a treasurer who meant to be repaid. {D} will not deny the mistakes, and asks the jury to look at all the facts."),
        closings: ("Eleven transfers to {D}'s personal card, $3,600 moved, a canceled bus charter, and spending on online shopping and a vacation rental. The trip money was not {D}'s.", "Uniform invoices that show {D} fronted $1,800 from personal funds, and a treasurer who meant to be repaid. The State must prove that {D} meant to steal rather than reimburse."),
        timeline: [(-60, "Trip deposits begin."), (-45, "Transfers to {DL}'s card begin."), (0, "The bus company cancels the charter."), (5, "The president reviews the statements.")],
        identified: "Account statements and a bus company notice.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "The kids missed the trip they saved for.")

    static let poolAfterHoursV1 = SmallCases.make(
