        openings: ("A private golf course closed at dusk on {DATE} with a notice at the cart gate. A gate camera recorded three cars arriving at 10 p.m., and security found three people with a cooler on the 14th green, including {D}.", "The defense will present a friend with a membership and a night pass for guests that evening, and a group that believed it was invited. A mistaken belief about an invitation is not a trespass by intent."),
        closings: ("A closing notice at the gate, three cars at 10 p.m., a cooler on the 14th green, and a text that said nobody checks the 14th fence. The group knew the course was closed.", "A member's night pass for guests, an invitation from a friend, and a group that did no harm. The State has not proved that {D} knew the entry was unauthorized."),
