        role: "State's witness in the cousin's case",
        exam: [.direct("Please describe your connection to the case.", "\"I am the State's eyewitness in a pending assault case against {D}'s cousin. I was named on the State's list two weeks earlier.\""), .direct("What did you find on {DATE}?", "\"A note under the wiper of my car outside a hair salon. It read, You don't need to be at the courthouse Monday. Think about your kids' bus stop.\""), .direct("What does the salon's lot camera show?", "\"{D} leaning over my windshield for ten seconds and walking off.\""), .direct("What was on the note?", "\"{D}'s fingerprint. It was on the paper.\""), .direct("How did the note make you feel?", "\"Terrified. It mentioned my children's bus stop. I called deputies and kept my children home.\""), .direct("Had you had contact with {D} before?", "\"No. There were no calls, texts, or social media contact from {D}. I did not know {D}.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} write the note?", "\"No. I only saw {D} at the windshield on the camera. I cannot say who wrote it.\""), .cross("Did the note threaten you directly?", "\"It said think about your kids' bus stop. It did not say what would happen, but I took it as a threat.\""), .cross("Does {D} get haircuts at that salon?", "\"I understand so. I did not know that before. {D} was there, and it could be a coincidence.\""), .cross("Did {D} say what the note meant?", "\"{D} says it asked me to tell the truth. That is not how I read it.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {D}'s cousin?", "\"No. I only know the cousin from the case. I did not speak to the cousin.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Salon coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How would you describe your job as a salon coworker?", "\"I work at the salon with the stylists. I see regular clients, including {D}, who gets a haircut every other week.\""), .direct("What do you know about {D}'s visits?", "\"{D} comes every other week. {D} is polite and friendly, and I have never seen {D} act aggressive.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} that day?", "\"Yes. {D} came for a haircut and left. I saw {D} walk to the lot.\""), .direct("How did {D} seem?", "\"Nervous, but calm. {D} said {D} wanted to ask {V} to tell the truth. I thought it was a plea.\""), .direct("Did {D} ever mention threatening {V}?", "\"No. {D} never said anything like that to me. I was shocked.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D}?", "\"Kind and a little shy. {D} cares about family, and I do not think {D} meant harm.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} leave the note?", "\"No. I did not. I only saw {D} in the lot from a distance.\""), .cross("Did you read the note?", "\"Later. I read it after deputies showed it to me. I was surprised by the wording.\""), .cross("Do you know about the cousin's case?", "\"A little. {D} told me about it. I do not know the details.\""), .cross("Could the note be a threat?", "\"It could be read as one. I cannot say what {D} meant.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about children?", "\"No. {D} never mentioned {V}'s children to me.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} slipped a veiled threat about a witness's children under a windshield wiper.", "A cousin's plea to tell the truth, taken the wrong way."),
        allocution: "\"I wrote it badly. I never meant to scare anyone.\"",
        truths: ("A jail call shows {DL}'s cousin telling {DL} to 'make {V.him} think about it' the day before.", "A second note, found later in {DL}'s car, read 'Please tell the truth. I'm sorry for the trouble.'"),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your cousin's case.", "\"My cousin is charged with assault. I believe my cousin is innocent. I have been very worried about the family.\""), .direct("Why did you leave a note?", "\"I wanted {V} to tell the truth. I asked {V} to think about my cousin's family, and I wrote the note poorly.\""), .direct("Did you mean the line about the bus stop?", "\"I meant to remind {V} of the effect on children, including my cousin's. I did not mean a threat.\""), .direct("What did your cousin say on the jail call?", "\"My cousin told me to make {V} think about it the day before. I should not have listened.\""), .direct("What about the second note?", "\"A second note in my car read, Please tell the truth. I'm sorry for the trouble. I wrote it, but did not leave it.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"The word for it is ashamed. I frightened someone. I did not mean to, and I am sorry.\""), .cross("You leaned over {V}'s windshield for ten seconds, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was leaving the note. The camera shows it.\""), .cross("Your fingerprint is on the note, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I wrote it and I touched it. I did not wear gloves.\""), .cross("The note said Think about your kids' bus stop, didn't it?", "\"Yes. I wrote that. I know how it reads, and I regret that.\""), .cross("Your cousin told you to make {V} think about it, didn't your cousin?", "\"Yes. On a jail call. I did what I was asked, and I made a mistake.\""), .cross("You get a haircut at that salon every other week, don't you?", "\"Yes. That is why I was there. I did not follow {V}.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} is the State's eyewitness in a pending assault case against {D}'s cousin. On {DATE}, {V} found a note under the wiper of {V}'s car outside a hair salon: You don't need to be at the courthouse Monday. Think about your kids' bus stop. The lot camera showed {D} at the car, and {D}'s fingerprint was on the paper.", "The defense will present a note that asked {V} to tell the truth, a second note that said please tell the truth, and a person who gets a haircut at that salon every other week. {D} did not mean a threat."),
        closings: ("A note that said think about your kids' bus stop, {D}'s fingerprint, a camera that shows ten seconds at the windshield, and a jail call from the cousin that said make {V} think about it. {V} was a witness.", "A plea to tell the truth, a second note that apologizes, and a person who gets a haircut at that salon. The State has not proved that {D} meant to intimidate a witness."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The State's list names {V}."), (0, "9:40 a.m.: {DL} is at the car."), (0, "11 a.m.: {V} finds the note."), (3, "{DL} is interviewed and charged.")],
        identified: "A lot camera and a fingerprint on a note.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I moved my kids to a new school. I testified anyway.",
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let inspectorBribeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.inspectorBribe",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Restaurant Owner Slides Prepaid Card Into Menu for Health Inspector", "Inspector's Phone Recorded Offer to Erase Grease Violation"],
        law: "bribery",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Offered a thing of value to {V}, a public official, to influence an official act, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A health inspector, {V}, was handed a menu on {DATE} with a $900 prepaid card tucked inside by {D}, a restaurant owner, who said, \"Make the grease trap violation go away.\" {V}'s phone recorded the visit at the request of investigators after earlier hints. {DL} says the card was a thank-you for a prior inspection.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Phone Recording", "{D}: 'Make the grease trap violation go away and there's more.'"), E(.physical, 3, "Prepaid Card", "A $900 prepaid card inside a menu.", .search), E(.document, 1, "Inspection Report", "A failing grease trap score on the day of the visit.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Thank-You", "{DL} says it was a thank-you for an earlier visit.")],
        role: "Health inspector",
        exam: [.direct("What does your work as a health inspector involve?", "\"I inspect restaurants for sanitation, grease control, and food safety. I score each visit and write a report, and I issue violations when something fails.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"{D}, a restaurant owner, handed me a menu with a $900 prepaid card tucked inside. {D} said, Make the grease trap violation go away.\""), .direct("Why was your phone recording?", "\"Investigators asked me to record the visit after earlier hints. I turned it on before I walked in.\""), .direct("What did {D} say on the recording?", "\"Make the grease trap violation go away and there's more. The words are clear.\""), .direct("What did your inspection find that day?", "\"A failing grease trap score. The trap had failed two earlier inspections.\""), .direct("What did you do with the card?", "\"I did not accept it. I reported it, and I gave the card and the recording to investigators.\""), .cross("Did {D} say the card was a thank-you?", "\"Yes. {D} says it was a thank-you for an earlier visit. It was not described that way on the recording.\""), .cross("Did {D} give gifts to others?", "\"I understand {D} gave a holiday gift set to every vendor and inspector. I did not see the set.\""), .cross("Did you receive a gift set before?", "\"I do not recall one. I do not accept gifts from restaurants.\""), .cross("Did the earlier hints come from {D}?", "\"Yes. {D} had made comments about helping out. I reported them.\""), .cross("Was the card a prepaid gift card?", "\"Yes. $900 prepaid. That is a large amount for a thank-you.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bribed an inspector to bury a violation.", "A thank-you to an inspector."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The trap had failed two earlier inspections.", "The card was part of a holiday gift set {DL} gave every vendor and inspector."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe your restaurant for the jury.", "\"I own a restaurant. I work hard, and I give gifts to vendors and inspectors during the holidays. It is a tradition.\""), .direct("What was the card?", "\"A gift card from a holiday set. I give one to everyone who helps us. I meant it as a thank-you for a prior inspection.\""), .direct("Why did you say make the grease trap violation go away?", "\"I was frustrated. I did not mean a bribe. I said it in a clumsy way, and I know it sounds bad.\""), .direct("Did you plan to bribe {V}?", "\"No. I did not. I wanted help understanding how to fix the trap. I should not have mentioned the card.\""), .direct("What about the trap's earlier failures?", "\"It failed twice. I was working on it. I had hired someone to fix it, and I was behind.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about it?", "\"Mostly I feel ashamed. I made a poor choice at a poor time. I did not mean to offer a bribe.\""), .cross("You handed {V} a menu with a $900 card inside, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know the amount is large.\""), .cross("You said there's more, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it. I meant more thanks, not more money for a favor.\""), .cross("The trap had failed two earlier inspections, hadn't it?", "\"Yes. I knew. I wanted more time to fix it.\""), .cross("The card was handed over during an inspection, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. That was bad timing. I see that now.\""), .cross("You asked {V} to make the violation go away, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know how it reads.\"")],
        openings: ("A health inspector, {V}, was handed a menu on {DATE} with a $900 prepaid card tucked inside by {D}, a restaurant owner, who said, Make the grease trap violation go away. {V}'s phone recorded the visit at the request of investigators.", "The defense will present a holiday gift set given to every vendor and inspector, a thank-you for an earlier visit, and a clumsy sentence. {D} did not mean to bribe {V}."),
        closings: ("A $900 card tucked in a menu, the words make the grease trap violation go away and there's more, and a failing trap score that day. The recording tells the story.", "A holiday gift set given to every vendor and inspector, and a clumsy sentence. The State must prove that {D} meant to bribe, and a thank-you is not a bribe."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The first failed inspection."), (-3, "The second failed inspection."), (0, "The visit and the menu.")],
        identified: "The inspector's phone recording.",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let parkSwingDamageV1 = SmallCases.make(
